## BINDING TEST DISCIPLINE (carried from today's gate kits)
1. A red seen under machine load is re-run ALONE 3 times before it is called a failure; the table prints all three results.
2. No chained step may wait on a marker that a cut-short earlier step would not write (EXIT-trap markers): every wait has a timeout that ends the chain with a printed reason, and a marker (done, exit code, heartbeat end) is written by a trap that runs on every exit path, or the chain does not wait on it.
3. `python3 -I` ignores `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`: **every python test run is `python3 -I -B`** (and `/usr/bin/python3 -I -B`). A stray `__pycache__` in a tree makes `test_resource_hygiene` fail on its own assertion. After every run, count `__pycache__` in the trees you ran in (expect 0; control: a planted directory counts 1); if one appears, MOVE it to quarantine and re-run that test alone.

